{"caller": "codex", "commit": "fc354847341e1f4820d9c0272aa27c77cd7a8c7e", "date": "2026-10-06T14:48:42+00:00", "exit": 0, "files": ["build-support/tests.nix", "conformance/corpus_shards.py", "conformance/native_binding_types.py", "conformance/native_binding_validation.py", "conformance/native_bindings.py", "conformance/native_call_recording.py", "conformance/native_record.py", "conformance/native_statements.py", "conformance/upstream_helpers.py", "conformance/upstream_selection.py", "plans/20261006-exact-tcl-values.status.md", "reviews/log.jsonl", "tests/conformance_fidelity_test.py", "tests/conformance_sampling_test.py", "tests/conformance_streaming_test.py", "tests/conformance_tcl_binding_policy_test.py", "tests/conformance_tcl_precision_test.py", "tests/conformance_upstream_test.py", "tests/nix_suites.json"], "findings": [{"id": "20261006T144842Z-fc354847#1", "line": 199, "path": "conformance/native_call_recording.py", "rule": "R10", "severity": "should", "text": "The new wrapper adds \"Capture this source case again, then freeze a new corpus\" to every validation failure, including an acquisition-time result mismatch from `check_source_results` (see `tests/conformance_tcl_precision_test.py:89`); there the error is a real fidelity difference, so a recapture cannot fix it and the advice misleads the user. Fix: give the recapture advice only for damaged or incomplete evidence fields, and pass fidelity differences from `check_source_results` through unchanged or with a message that says the case is excluded."}, {"id": "20261006T144842Z-fc354847#2", "line": 124, "path": "conformance/native_bindings.py", "rule": "R1", "severity": "should", "text": "The read-only policy is only half named: `READ_ONLY_TCL_HELPERS` covers `onecolumn` and `exists`, but every call site still adds the literal `helper.startswith(\"aux:\")` rule (`native_statements.py:60`, `native_record.py:155`, `upstream_helpers.py:39`), and the docstring does not mention that `aux:` helpers are also read-only. Fix: define one named predicate with a docstring, for example `is_read_only_tcl_helper(helper)`, that covers both rules, and use it at all three call sites."}, {"id": "20261006T144842Z-fc354847#3", "line": 84, "path": "conformance/corpus_shards.py", "rule": "R4", "severity": "should", "text": "`validate_recording` now turns every `KeyError`, `TypeError` and `IndexError` into a `ValueError`, so this changed `except (KeyError, TypeError, IndexError)` branch and its new message can never run. Fix: remove the dead `try`/`except` around `validate_recording` and let its `ValueError`, which already names the case, pass through."}], "id": "20261006T144842Z-fc354847", "kind": "review", "reviewer": "claude", "revision": "@-", "rules": {"R1": "62d446279093", "R10": "638d8cbd1df8", "R11": "5de19cdbbbc1", "R12": "99f66579f467", "R13": "da0926dafb88", "R2": "e5e78fb2a52a", "R3": "4f9188eadd60", "R4": "ea7ca17539eb", "R5": "b8613a2d693b", "R6": "5600dce59aef", "R7": "0b68df581c57", "R8": "b4168359c60d", "R9": "5a69196344d0"}, "well_formed": true}
